{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["אשר חלב זבחימו יאכלו — the elohim of Israel." "He will conceal — He would conceal you in His shadow [if there were any power in His hand to help His people who offer sacrifices to Him and look to Him for salvation], and His kindness as formerly, when they trusted in Him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Rashbam reads the verse's rhetorical challenge as referring to Israel's own false gods: let those gods save them. The lemma's pronoun is thus redirected: 'their gods' = the gods of Israel.", 1 "The bracketed clause is in brackets in the source; preserved as such."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:57.859215346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}